# Go build output
/platformkit
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Local configuration and secrets. config.yaml is unanchored for the same reason
# data/ is, and apps/platformkit/config.yaml is named as well because that is
# where somebody following the README's `cd apps/platformkit` puts one.
config.yaml
apps/platformkit/config.yaml
.env

# Dependencies. There is no generated stylesheet to ignore: the CSS is a Go
# value, built by ui.Stylesheet and served from memory. See ui/ui.go.
node_modules/
e2e/node_modules/
e2e/test-results/
e2e/playwright-report/

# The browser run's own status file. `make e2e` writes one wherever Playwright ran
# from, and it records the outcome of a run rather than anything a build reads.
# The repository root is where the kernel's own run lands, so it is named as well.
/test-results/

# Uploaded bytes. config.example.yaml puts them here, so a laptop needs no
# absolute path and a container mounts a volume at it; see kit/config.Files.
#
# Unanchored, because the path is relative to whatever the process's working
# directory is: `make run` starts the app in apps/platformkit, so it writes
# apps/platformkit/data/, and a root-anchored /data/ ignored none of it. A
# review found an uploaded file staged for commit.
data/

# Scratch space
.tmp/

# Python (tooling only)
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Editor junk
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
